# ---------------------------------------------------------------- solardata

# data/processed holds generated artefacts. Two of them ARE committed and must be
# un-ignored explicitly:
#
#   quality_report.md / .json  the human review artefact. Organised per station,
#                              small enough to read in a pull request, and the
#                              acceptance test for a data change: a change that
#                              moves the numbers shows up here as a diff a
#                              reviewer can read, rather than as a count that
#                              moved.
#
# solardata.db is about 85 MiB after VACUUM (104 MiB as the ingest leaves it),
# which is over GitHub's 100 MiB per-file limit, so it cannot be committed. It
# ships as a GitHub Release asset instead; see .github/workflows/release.yml.
# Locally: make build (or \python -m etl all\).
#
# 0.9 removed the committed \parquet/\ interchange tree along with the stage
# that wrote it and \scripts/parquet_manifest.py\. A fifth build stage with its
# own manifest comparison and its own pyarrow dependency is not a fifth thing
# this dataset needs; the SQLite file is the distribution channel.
data/processed/*
!data/processed/quality_report.md
!data/processed/quality_report.json

# public/data is NOT ignored: it is the static data the site fetches, generated
# by \python -m etl export\ and 3.3 MiB, of which most is the hourly rollups. A
# rebuild produces a readable diff, and committing it means the GitHub Pages
# deploy works from the repository alone with no build step on the server.
#
# Each station's CSVs hold only that station's channels, so a station with five
# real channels ships five channels rather than 30 columns of NULL -- which is
# most of why this fell from 5.6 MiB to 3.3.

# The retired 0.8 export location. 0.9 writes public/data and nothing else;
# --export-dir still redirects it, so the directory can appear in a working copy.
data/exports/

# The raw archive under data/raw IS committed: it is the primary source of
# truth and must never be regenerated. If you ever need to exclude it, do it
# here deliberately, not by accident.

# Python bytecode and build output from the etl package
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
